 "notes": "Archive only: no Isaac process, no episode, no model call; labels, windows and the gate were committed (19666343) before the audit read any outcome. Registered screen: failures that follow a healthy hand-back (reconstructed trigger; predicate true and centred on the 10 steps ending at the end of support, step 183, or the end of the stroke boost, step 243; first loss within 30 steps) are 48 of 3,072 JOINT cases in R-124 (0.0156, 95% [0.011, 0.020]) and 67 of 4,096 in R-126 (0.0164 [0.012, 0.020]); the transplant has 40 of 4,096 (0.0098). Both JOINT upper bounds are far below 0.06: REFUTED, and simulation is not eligible. A 60-step window gives 55 and 88 (0.018, 0.021); a 15-step window 38 and 45. Where JOINT's 626 R-124 failures are instead: 239 never triggered (94 early drops, 42 persistent slow, 69 intermittent or near miss, 30 off-centre); 97 triggered and never rolled again after support (63 persistent slow, 31 late drops); 222 triggered and rolled at some point after support but were not rolling steadily at either boundary (147 persistent slow, 63 intermittent or near miss); 20 lost rolling more than 30 steps after a healthy boundary (15 near miss); 48 reachable (28 persistent slow, 19 intermittent or near miss). The same proportions hold in R-126. So the dominant triggered failure is a re-capture that does not produce steady rolling by the time support and boost end, not a good state lost at hand-back; and persistent-slow and intermittent/near-miss failures do not share one cause (near misses are mostly untriggered or late). Reconstruction: 1,191 reconstructed first-episode triggers against 1,236 recorded (which include later auto-reset episodes) in R-124, 1,597 vs 1,658 and 1,545 vs 1,596 in R-126; no cell's reconstruction exceeds its recorded upper bound; moving the window one step later changes 8 trigger flags per archive and the reachable counts by at most 1. Individual flags are reconstructed, not recorded. Excursion from the protocol text, stated in triage: the module is lares/envs/isaac_pen_spin/recovery_handback_audit.py (the study registry resolves modules there), not scripts/. Timing was read off the frozen module code: decision at step 149, support 35 steps (boundary index 183), boost 60 steps (boundary index 243). Associations only: nothing here shows what an intervention would recover."
